# Privacy Policy — WHOOP Health AI

**Last updated: November 6, 2026**

## 1. Introduction

WHOOP Health AI is a personal health analytics project designed to help its developer review and understand health, recovery, sleep, and activity information obtained from WHOOP.

The application is currently intended for private testing by its developer. It is not currently offered to patients or the general public.

## 2. Information Accessed

With the account holder's authorization, the application may access the following WHOOP information:

- Recovery scores and heart rate variability (HRV)
- Resting heart rate
- Daily physiological cycles and strain
- Sleep duration and sleep-related metrics
- Workout and physical activity information

Access is limited to the permissions granted through WHOOP authorization.

## 3. Purpose of Processing

The information is used to develop and test personal health summaries, identify trends, and evaluate potential personalized reporting features.

The application does not provide medical diagnoses or replace professional medical advice.

## 4. Data Storage and Security

During initial development, the application will not intentionally publish personal WHOOP health information in public repositories.

Before any persistent storage or automated processing is enabled, appropriate access controls, secure storage, and data protection measures must be implemented.

WHOOP account passwords are not collected by this application.

## 5. Data Sharing

The application is currently intended for use by its developer only.

It is not intended to sell personal health information or make it available to other users.

Any future integration with third-party processing services will require an updated privacy policy describing the services and data transfers involved.

## 6. User Control

The account holder may revoke the application's access through the available WHOOP authorization controls.

Any personal data retained by the application must be handled in accordance with applicable privacy requirements.

## 7. Future Development

WHOOP Health AI may later be developed into a multi-user application for healthcare-related monitoring and reporting.

Before other users or patients are enrolled, this policy must be updated to explain the actual processing activities, consent procedures, retention periods, deletion procedures, data recipients, and applicable privacy rights.

Additional legal and security requirements will be assessed before such use.

## 8. Changes to This Policy

This policy may be updated as the application's functionality and data-processing practices evolve.

## 9. Contact

For privacy-related inquiries, contact the application developer using the verified contact email listed in the WHOOP Developer Portal.
